title The two readings that disagree about what prose is
prompt Baton -- Petrichor seat, docs-geode lane, unattended lap 4188.
rota lap 4188, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; care and flow, read up close. Its threshold asks a lap to swallow the page rather than measure it from a distance, which is exactly what found the door's opening paragraph: four coined words in two sentences, none given its plain function, on the page a newcomer opens first. Gall's half of the fixed seat named the repair -- grow the shelf's door from the smaller thing that already worked, the three doors a reader actually takes.
think Cold roster answered guards_red=3, and the roster scan's own evidence named the other two -- readme_reach and reds_fold -- neither of which printed in this run's own lines. Read construction/standing-equipment-reds/readme_reach.txt: broken_in_living=1, construction/ITINERARY.md -> archive/REDS-a-label-is-not-its-target-rows-571.md.
think That shelf is rows-570 on disk; rows-571 is the pen row, cited correctly one block down. reds_fold reds because it runs the same reach scan, and standing_equipment reds because it records both. One root, three red rows -- REDS %524 exactly, its fifth firing, since an archive-shelf citation matches none of the three commit-time link walls.
think Reds first, so line 53 was repaired before any new work. All three guards then green.
think Then the lane. Graded every docs-geode door: all at or above B, so no molt frame was forced. The shelf's own front door read lowest at B 84, and its weakness was Reach rather than Truth -- grade 11 against a Door ceiling of 9 over 112 counted words.
think Read it as a newcomer. The opening paragraph after "What this is" ran: fascial waves -- Grain years -- feed this shelf; MUR, Tally, and weave rounds then crush it. Four coined terms, none given the plain function Gauge asks for on first use, and no sentence anywhere saying which door to open first.
think Rewrote the opening to name three doors in the order a reader takes them -- the first hour, the study guide, the library index -- and to give crush and wave their Lexicon meanings in ordinary words: crush means compile, a wave is a Grain year.
obs The first rewrite made the grade WORSE. Reach fell 70 -> 60 and the counted word total dropped 112 -> 82, while Register rose 89 -> 92 on the same text. The two readings were seeing different pages.
obs The cause is one regex. prose_register_scan.sh skips a bullet the CommonMark way -- marker THEN whitespace -- after REDS %451 proved the elder form read **Bold** paragraph openings as bullets. The Reach awk inside qa_report_card.sh still spells the elder form, and its own comment claims the hold-out is "the same call reference_block.awk makes for Register", which that file never made -- it decides reference tables.
obs Measured by running both line rules side by side over 5,549 tracked Markdown files outside gratitude/ and vendor/: 22,041 body lines across 4,120 files are counted by Register and dropped by Reach.
obs Did NOT widen it. Correcting the rule re-grades every graded page in one unmeasured step, and qa_report_card.sh already refuses that shape by name for its link count. A lap that corrects its own grader moves a ceiling by a side door, so the row is booked OPEN and the question goes to Keaton.
obs The send met a moved xy/main. A peer had spent %572 and %573 while this round ran, so the unshared row renumbered to %574 -- the derived spine working exactly as written, and the reason rule 4 says cite by stamp until the number is bound. Nothing outside the ledger had spelled it.
obs Both pins returned from that rebase at their ceilings. REDS left 520 bytes of slack for a three-field row and the card left none, so the row was cut from 2,051 bytes to 545 and the card block rewritten to the elder's own size. The OPEN set has outgrown the 8 ships x 4,096 that sized the REDS bound; named on the card rather than raised here.
obs Wrote the two paragraphs to open with an ordinary word instead of a bold key, which is better Door prose anyway. Reach 80, composite B+ 87, and no claim on the page changed.
